/* Manu Tere · zh · pack aus · generated by build.py; loaded with the pack */
__mtLangPack('zh','aus',{"Seen from above: a humpback whale and her calf off Rurutu, and your small boat":"从上方俯瞰：Rurutu 外海的一头座头鲸和她的幼鲸，还有你的小船","July to October: humpback whales come to Rurutu to give birth and raise their calves. You go out with a licensed guide in a small boat. <b>How do you approach the mother and her calf?</b>":"7 月到 10 月，座头鲸来到 Rurutu 生育和抚养幼鲸。你和一位持证向导乘小船出海。<b>你要怎样接近鲸妈妈和她的幼鲸？</b>","From the side, on a parallel course":"从侧面，沿平行航线","Straight at them, head-on":"迎面直冲过去","From behind, to follow them":"从后面跟着它们","Never head-on: it blocks their way and frightens them.":"绝不能迎面接近：这会挡住它们的去路，吓到它们。","Never from behind: it feels like a chase.":"绝不能从后面接近：那就像在追赶它们。","<b>Approach from the side.</b> Hold the throttle to go forward. Inside the {#1} m circle, stay <b>under {#2} knots</b>. Stop the engine just outside the {#3} m circle.":"<b>从侧面接近。</b>按住油门前进。进入 {#1} m 范围后，速度要保持<b>在 {#2} 节以下</b>。在 {#3} m 圈外面一点就关掉引擎。","Hold: throttle":"按住：油门","Stop the engine":"关掉引擎","Still too far to see much: come a little closer, slowly.":"还太远，看不清楚：慢慢地再靠近一点。","They surface again further on. Try once more, gently.":"它们在更远处又浮出了水面。再轻轻地试一次。","<b>Engine off.</b> You drift quietly. The mother rests just under the surface; the calf rises every few minutes to breathe, and plays.":"<b>引擎关了。</b>你静静地漂着。鲸妈妈在水面下休息；幼鲸每隔几分钟浮上来换气，还在嬉戏。","The calf turns and swims toward your boat, curious. What do you do?":"幼鲸转过身，好奇地朝你的船游来。你怎么做？","Stay still and quiet, and let it come and go":"保持安静不动，让它自由来去","Yes. The calf decides. Never move toward it, never touch it, and never come between it and its mother.":"对。由幼鲸自己决定。绝不要朝它移动，绝不要触摸它，也绝不要插到它和妈妈之间。","Start the engine to follow it":"发动引擎去跟着它","No: whales must never be chased.":"不行：绝不能追赶鲸鱼。","Jump in to touch it":"跳下水去摸它","Never. Touching is forbidden and the mother protects her calf.":"绝对不行。禁止触摸，而且鲸妈妈会保护她的幼鲸。","You watched a mother and her calf{A}, the way the guides of Rurutu do. In French Polynesia, all whales and dolphins are protected: inside 300 m boats slow down and come alongside, they never chase, cut in front or come between a mother and calf, and only licensed operators may take swimmers in the water. The rules were made stricter in 2025.":"你像 Rurutu 的向导那样，观赏了一头鲸妈妈和她的幼鲸{A}。在法属波利尼西亚，所有鲸和海豚都受到保护：在 300 m 范围内，船只要减速并从侧面靠近，绝不追赶、绝不抢到前方，也绝不插到母鲸和幼鲸之间；只有持证经营者才能带游客下水。这些规定在 2025 年变得更加严格。","Distance: {A} m":"距离：{A} m","Speed: {A} knots":"速度：{A} 节","Too fast inside {#1} m! The mother dives and leads her calf away.":"在 {#1} m 范围内开得太快了！鲸妈妈潜入水中，带着幼鲸离开了。","Too close! Inside {#1} m the mother feels threatened: she dives with her calf.":"太近了！在 {#1} m 范围内，鲸妈妈感到威胁：她带着幼鲸潜走了。","Slow down…":"减速……","Good distance. Stop the engine now.":"距离正好。现在关掉引擎。","Outside {#1} m you may go a little faster.":"在 {#1} m 以外，你可以开得稍快一点。","Slow and steady.":"慢慢地，稳稳地。","The monster’s mouth":"怪兽之口","Rows of columns, where stalactites from the roof have joined stalagmites from the floor: they look like the teeth of a great mouth. This is why Te Ana Taupeʻe is called the monster’s mouth.":"一排排石柱，是洞顶的钟乳石和地面的石笋连在一起形成的：它们看起来就像一张大嘴里的牙齿。这就是 Te Ana Taupeʻe 被称为怪兽之口的原因。","A growing stalactite":"正在生长的钟乳石","A drop of water hangs at its tip. Each drop leaves a tiny ring of limestone: a stalactite grows only a few millimetres in a lifetime.":"一滴水挂在它的尖端。每一滴水都会留下一圈细小的石灰岩：一根钟乳石在人的一生中只能长几毫米。","Shells in the rock":"岩石里的贝壳","Rurutu’s cliffs are an old coral reef pushed up out of the sea, called makatea. Look closely: old shells and corals are set in the stone.":"Rurutu 的悬崖是一片从海里被抬升起来的古老珊瑚礁，叫做 makatea。仔细看：古老的贝壳和珊瑚就嵌在石头里。","A stone curtain":"石帘","Where water runs down the wall, the limestone forms folds like a curtain. Tap it gently with a fingernail? No: even a touch leaves skin oil that stops it growing.":"在水沿着岩壁流下的地方，石灰岩形成了像帘子一样的褶皱。用指甲轻轻敲一敲？不行：哪怕只是碰一下，皮肤上的油脂也会让它停止生长。","Roots from above":"从上方垂下的根","The roots of trees growing on the cliff top push through cracks to reach water, hanging down into the dark.":"生长在悬崖顶上的树，把根伸进裂缝去寻找水源，一直垂进黑暗里。","Inside Te Ana Taupeʻe, a limestone cave of Rurutu, lit by a torch":"在 Rurutu 的石灰岩洞穴 Te Ana Taupeʻe 里，被手电筒照亮","With a guide from Moerai you enter Te Ana Taupeʻe. Move the torch around the cave and tap what you find. <b>Look, but never touch or break anything.</b>":"你和一位来自 Moerai 的向导走进 Te Ana Taupeʻe。在洞里移动手电筒，点击你发现的东西。<b>只看，绝不触摸，也绝不弄坏任何东西。</b>","Your manu spots a little broken stalactite, as long as a finger, and would like to keep it as a souvenir…":"你的 manu 发现了一小截断掉的钟乳石，有手指那么长，想把它留作纪念……","Leave it in the cave":"把它留在洞里","Slip it in the bag":"把它塞进包里","Right: everything in a cave belongs to the cave. The guide nods.":"对：洞里的一切都属于洞穴。向导点了点头。","No: it took thousands of years to form, and the cave must stay whole for the next visitors.":"不行：它花了几千年才形成，洞穴必须完整地留给以后的游客。","You explored Te Ana Taupeʻe with your torch and left it as you found it. Rurutu is a raised island: its old coral reef rose out of the sea and now forms cliffs full of caves, the ana. Some were shelters, others burial places: go only with a guide.":"你拿着手电筒探索了 Te Ana Taupeʻe，并让它保持原样。Rurutu 是一座隆起岛：它古老的珊瑚礁从海中升起，如今形成了布满洞穴（ana）的悬崖。有些洞穴曾是避难所，有些则是墓地：一定要跟着向导去。","On the village green, at the end of the Tere, a big round stone waits to be lifted":"在村子的草地上，Tere 的终点，一块大圆石等着被举起来","Every January, the people of Rurutu go around their island together: the <b>Tere</b>. At each stop an <span>ʻōrero</span> tells the stories of the place. At the end comes the <b>amoraʻa ʻōfaʻi</b>: lifting a heavy stone onto the shoulder. Which stone will your manu try?":"每年 1 月，Rurutu 的人们会一起环岛而行：这就是 <b>Tere</b>。在每一站，都有一位 <span>ʻōrero</span> 讲述当地的故事。最后是 <b>amoraʻa ʻōfaʻi</b>：把一块沉重的石头举上肩头。你的 manu 要试哪一块石头？","The champions’ stone, about {#1} kg":"冠军之石，约 {#1} kg","The crowd laughs kindly: that one is for the strongest men and women of the island. Your manu tries anyway… it does not move! Let’s take the small one.":"人群善意地笑了：那块是给岛上最强壮的男人和女人的。你的 manu 还是试了一下……石头纹丝不动！我们还是选小的吧。","Lift to the beat of the pahu drum: <b>tap “Lift!” when the red ring meets the black one.</b> Knees, then belly, then up on the shoulder. Miss, and the stone slips down.":"跟着 pahu 鼓的节拍举起：<b>当红圈与黑圈重合时，点击“举起！”。</b>先到膝盖，再到腹部，然后上肩。错过节拍，石头就会滑下来。","Lift!":"举起！","To the knees!":"到膝盖！","To the belly!":"到腹部！","On the shoulder!":"上肩！","on the first try":"第一次尝试就","Your manu lifted the stone onto its shoulder{A}, and the crowd of the Tere cheers. On Rurutu, the island tour of January ends with the amoraʻa ʻōfaʻi: men and women lift stones of up to about 150 kg onto their shoulders, as their ancestors did.":"你的 manu {A}把石头扛上了肩头，Tere 的人群欢呼起来。在 Rurutu，1 月的环岛之行以 amoraʻa ʻōfaʻi 结束：男人和女人像他们的祖先一样，把重达约 150 kg 的石头举上肩头。","Off the beat: the stone slips. Wait for the rings to meet.":"没跟上节拍：石头滑下来了。等两个圈重合再点。","ʻUra, the Rimatara lorikeet":"ʻUra，Rimatara 吸蜜鹦鹉","Common myna":"家八哥","Flowering trees and coconut palms of Rimatara":"Rimatara 开花的树和椰子树","The <span>ʻura</span> drinks nectar from flowers and coconut blossoms. Watch the trees and <b>tap each ʻura</b> when it lands: red breast, green wings, a blue cap. Other birds visit too.":"<span>ʻura</span> 吸食花朵和椰子花的花蜜。注意观察树上，每当有 ʻura 落下就<b>点击它</b>：红胸脯、绿翅膀、蓝色的头顶。也有别的鸟会来。","An ʻura! Red as its name.":"一只 ʻura！和它的名字一样红。","There it is, drinking nectar.":"它在那儿，正在吸花蜜。","Another one, quick and noisy.":"又一只，又快又吵。","A visitor would like to take an ʻura home in a cage. What do you say?":"有位游客想把一只 ʻura 装进笼子带回家。你怎么说？","No: it is protected, and must stay on Rimatara":"不行：它受到保护，必须留在 Rimatara","Yes. A royal tabu has protected the ʻura since about {#1}. It may not be caught, hurt or taken away.":"对。大约从 {#1} 年起，ʻura 就受到一道王室禁令（tabu）的保护。不得捕捉、伤害或带走它。","Yes, if it is a young one":"可以，如果是只小鸟的话","No: no ʻura may ever be taken.":"不行：任何 ʻura 都永远不能被带走。","Only a few feathers":"只拿几根羽毛","No: the birds must not be caught or harmed at all.":"不行：这些鸟完全不能被捕捉或伤害。","You counted five ʻura. Rimatara has no rats, which eat eggs and chicks; the lorikeet lives on here while it vanished from other islands. The last queen of Rimatara declared it tabu, and in {#1} a few birds were taken to Atiu in the Cook Islands, with Rimatara’s agreement, to found a second home.":"你数到了五只 ʻura。Rimatara 没有会吃鸟蛋和雏鸟的老鼠；这种吸蜜鹦鹉在别的岛上消失了，却在这里存活了下来。Rimatara 的最后一位女王宣布它为 tabu。{#1} 年，经 Rimatara 同意，几只鸟被带到库克群岛的 Atiu，建立了第二个家园。","That’s a myna, a bird brought from Asia. Not an ʻura.":"那是一只家八哥，从亚洲引进的鸟。不是 ʻura。","That’s the Rimatara reed warbler, another bird found only here. Not an ʻura.":"那是 Rimatara 苇莺，另一种只生活在这里的鸟。不是 ʻura。","Yellow, wilting leaves: the potatoes below are ready.":"叶子发黄、枯萎：下面的土豆可以收了。","Still green and growing: the potatoes are too small.":"还是绿的，还在长：土豆还太小。","An orange shoulder shows at the soil: pull it!":"土里露出了橙色的顶部：拔出来！","No orange showing yet: it needs more weeks.":"还没有露出橙色：还要再长几周。","Thick and tall: a fine leek.":"又粗又高：一根好韭葱。","Thin as a pencil: let it grow.":"细得像铅笔：让它再长长。","Rows of vegetables on Tubuai":"Tubuai 的一排排蔬菜","Tubuai is cooler than Tahiti: potatoes, carrots and leeks grow here, which is why it is called a granary of French Polynesia. <b>Harvest only what is ready.</b>":"Tubuai 比 Tahiti 凉爽：土豆、胡萝卜和韭葱都能在这里生长，所以它被称为法属波利尼西亚的粮仓。<b>只收获已经成熟的。</b>","Pack the crates for Papeete":"为 Papeete 装箱","Your crates go to the airport and the cargo ship. Thanks to its cooler climate, Tubuai grows vegetables of temperate lands, potatoes, carrots, leeks, cabbages, as well as taro: much of it is sold in Tahiti.":"你的箱子被送往机场和货轮。得益于较凉爽的气候，Tubuai 能种植温带地区的蔬菜，比如土豆、胡萝卜、韭葱、卷心菜，还有芋头：大部分都销往 Tahiti。","A marae of Tubuai being restored: a low wall of stones, some fallen in the grass":"Tubuai 一座正在修复的 marae：一道矮石墙，有些石头倒在草地上","With the island’s heritage team, you help restore a marae, a sacred place of the ancestors. <b>Tap a fallen stone, then the gap in the wall where it fits.</b>":"你和岛上的文化遗产团队一起修复一座 marae，那是祖先的圣地。<b>先点击一块倒下的石头，再点击墙上它能嵌进去的缺口。</b>","It fits.":"正好合适。","The wall is whole again. Now raise the standing stone.":"墙又完整了。现在把立石竖起来。","Not that gap: look at the size and shape.":"不是那个缺口：看看大小和形状。","The marae is restored. A visitor wants a photo standing on the wall. What do you say?":"marae 修复好了。有位游客想站在墙上拍照。你怎么说？","Not on the stones: take the photo from the ground, with respect":"不要站到石头上：站在地面上拍照，以示尊重","Yes. A marae is a sacred place: never climb on it or move its stones.":"对。marae 是圣地：绝不要爬上去，也不要移动它的石头。","Yes, it is strong now":"可以，现在它很结实了","No: climbing on a marae is disrespectful, restored or not.":"不行：不管修复与否，爬上 marae 都是不敬的。","You helped put a marae back together. On Tubuai, the marae were places of the chiefs’ councils and of ceremonies; in {#1} the Culture and Heritage Service restored one of them with the people of the island. Visit marae with a guide, and never climb on them or take a stone.":"你帮忙把一座 marae 重新砌好了。在 Tubuai，marae 曾是酋长议事和举行仪式的地方；{#1} 年，文化与遗产局和岛上居民一起修复了其中一座。参观 marae 要跟着向导，绝不要爬上去或拿走石头。","Under a shelter on Raivavae, a canoe hull and a new plank to sew on":"在 Raivavae 的一座棚子下，一个独木舟船体和一块要缝上去的新木板","Raivavae is the only island of French Polynesia where canoes are still <b>sewn</b>: planks are tied to the carved hull with cord. <b>{#1}. Shave the plank</b> with the adze so its edge fits the hull. Hold, and release in the green zone.":"Raivavae 是法属波利尼西亚唯一一座至今仍在<b>缝制</b>独木舟的岛：用绳子把木板绑在雕凿好的船体上。<b>{#1}. 刨削木板</b>，用锛子把它的边缘修得和船体严丝合缝。按住，在绿色区域松开。","Hold to shave":"按住刨削","Not yet: the plank still rocks on the hull.":"还不行：木板在船体上还会晃动。","Too much! A gap opens. Take a new plank and try again.":"刨太多了！出现了缝隙。换一块新木板再试一次。","<b>{#1}. Drill the holes</b> in pairs, one in the plank, one in the hull edge. Tap each mark.":"<b>{#1}. 钻孔</b>，成对地钻，一个在木板上，一个在船体边缘。点击每个标记。","<b>{#1}. Lash, <span>nati</span>:</b> pass the coconut-fibre cord through each pair of holes and pull it tight.":"<b>{#1}. 捆绑，<span>nati</span>：</b>把椰纤绳穿过每一对孔，拉紧。","Lash and pull tight":"捆绑并拉紧","<b>{#1}. Seal the seam</b> so the sea stays out: press fibre and gum along it, from bow to stern.":"<b>{#1}. 密封接缝</b>，不让海水进来：从船头到船尾，沿接缝压入纤维和树胶。","Seal the seam":"密封接缝","Launch it on the lagoon":"在泻湖上下水","The new plank is sewn on. Time to see if it floats dry!":"新木板缝好了。来看看它下水后会不会漏水吧！","Your sewn plank holds, and not a drop comes in. Before nails and screws, canoes across Polynesia were built this way: planks shaped with stone adzes and sewn together with sennit cord. Raivavae still keeps the skill alive.":"你缝上的木板很牢固，一滴水也没渗进来。在有钉子和螺丝之前，整个波利尼西亚的独木舟都是这样造的：用石锛削出木板，再用椰纤绳缝在一起。Raivavae 至今仍保留着这门手艺。","The white sand of motu Vaiamanu, the swimming-pool motu of Raivavae":"Vaiamanu 小岛（motu）的白沙滩，Raivavae 的“游泳池小岛”","On motu Vaiamanu, the “swimming-pool motu”, the women of Raivavae gather tiny shells for necklaces. <b>Pick up only empty shells:</b> some are still somebody’s home.":"在 Vaiamanu 小岛，也就是“游泳池小岛”上，Raivavae 的女人们收集小贝壳来做项链。<b>只捡空贝壳：</b>有些贝壳里还住着别人呢。","Legs! A hermit crab lives in this one. Put it down gently.":"有腿！这个里面住着一只寄居蟹。轻轻放下它。","Empty and shiny: into the basket.":"空的，还闪闪发亮：放进篮子。","<b>Now string them</b>, following the pattern of the mama who teaches you: one white cowry, one golden cone…":"<b>现在把它们串起来</b>，按照教你的那位 mama 的图案：一个白色宝贝螺，一个金色芋螺……","White cowry":"白色宝贝螺","Golden cone":"金色芋螺","Look at the pattern again.":"再看一遍图案。","Your hei pūpū is finished, and your manu wears it proudly. On Raivavae, women make necklaces of tiny shells from the motu, as well as hats, mats and tīfaifai quilts. Take only empty shells, and never take living ones from the lagoon.":"你的 hei pūpū 做好了，你的 manu 骄傲地戴上了它。在 Raivavae，女人们用 motu 上的小贝壳制作项链，还编帽子、席子，缝 tīfaifai 拼布被。只捡空贝壳，绝不要从泻湖里拿走活的贝。","Flooded taro terraces in a valley of Rapa":"Rapa 山谷里灌满水的芋头梯田","On Rapa, taro grows in flooded terraces, and becomes <span>pōpoi</span>, the island’s staple. <b>{#1}. Pull up the ripe taro</b>: their leaves are turning yellow.":"在 Rapa，芋头种在灌满水的梯田里，然后做成 <span>pōpoi</span>，这是岛上的主食。<b>{#1}. 拔出成熟的芋头</b>：它们的叶子正在变黄。","Green and strong: not ready yet.":"又绿又壮：还没熟。","<b>{#1}. Cook the taro</b> in the earth oven, covered with leaves and hot stones, for hours.":"<b>{#1}. 煮芋头</b>：放进地炉，盖上叶子和热石头，焖上几个小时。","<b>{#1}. Peel</b> the cooked taro while it is warm.":"<b>{#1}. 剥皮</b>：趁热剥去煮熟芋头的皮。","<b>{#1}. Pound it</b> on the board with the stone pounder, the <span>penu</span>. When the paste gets too stiff, add a little water.":"<b>{#1}. 捣碎</b>：在木板上用石杵 <span>penu</span> 捣。芋头糊太硬时，加一点水。","A little water":"加一点水","Too stiff to pound: add a little water.":"太硬了捣不动：加一点水。","Getting stiff…":"变硬了……","<b>{#1}. Wrap it in leaves</b> and leave it to sour for a few days. Sour pōpoi keeps a long time: food for the cold months, and for long voyages.":"<b>{#1}. 用叶子包起来</b>，放几天让它发酸。发酸的 pōpoi 能保存很久：是寒冷月份的食物，也是远航的干粮。","Your pōpoi is ready: smooth, a little sour, and it keeps for a long time. On Rapa, families still work together in the taro terraces and make pōpoi together. They give you a bundle of it for your canoe.":"你的 pōpoi 做好了：细腻、微酸，能保存很久。在 Rapa，家家户户至今仍一起在芋头梯田里劳作，一起做 pōpoi。他们送你一包，让你带上独木舟。","The ridge of Rapa, with the terraces of an old hill fort on the summit":"Rapa 的山脊，山顶上有一座古老山顶要塞的梯田","With a guide from Haurei you climb to Morongo Uta, a fort on the ridge built about 500 years ago. <b>Which way?</b> ({A} / 4)":"你和一位来自 Haurei 的向导爬上 Morongo Uta，这是一座约 500 年前建在山脊上的要塞。<b>走哪条路？</b>（{A} / 4）","Follow the ridge path, as the guide does":"像向导一样沿着山脊小路走","Cut across the steep grass slope":"横穿陡峭的草坡","Take the shortcut by the cliff edge":"走悬崖边的捷径","Climb the loose stones of the old wall":"爬上旧墙松动的石头","Never climb the old walls: they are part of the fort.":"绝不要攀爬古老的墙：它们是要塞的一部分。","Too dangerous: the slopes of Rapa are steep and the wind is strong.":"太危险了：Rapa 的山坡很陡，风也很大。","From the summit you see the terraces of the fort, where houses stood, and the deep bay below. Something green moves in a tree… <b>Can you spot the <span>koko</span></b>, the Rapa fruit dove?":"从山顶上，你能看到要塞的梯田，那里曾经有房屋，下面是深深的海湾。树上有个绿色的东西在动……<b>你能找到 <span>koko</span></b>，也就是 Rapa 果鸠吗？","The koko! The largest fruit dove of French Polynesia, found only on Rapa. Only about {#1} are left.":"是 koko！法属波利尼西亚最大的果鸠，只生活在 Rapa。现在只剩下大约 {#1} 只了。","Back down at the bay, a sign says this reef is under rāhui. What do you do?":"回到海湾，一块牌子写着这片礁石正处于 rāhui 之下。你怎么做？","Fish somewhere else and let the reef rest":"去别处钓鱼，让礁石休养","Yes. The elders of Rapa close places to fishing for a time, so that fish and shellfish can grow back.":"对。Rapa 的长老们会在一段时间内禁止在某些地方捕鱼，让鱼和贝类重新长起来。","Fish quietly, just a little":"悄悄地钓，就钓一点点","No: a rāhui means nobody takes anything there until it is lifted.":"不行：rāhui 意味着在解禁之前，谁都不能从那里拿走任何东西。","You climbed to Morongo Uta, saw the koko and respected the rāhui. Rapa once had more than a dozen fortified villages on its ridges, with terraces and ditches cut into the mountain. Today a council of elders still looks after the land, and rāhui protect the reefs.":"你爬上了 Morongo Uta，看到了 koko，还遵守了 rāhui。Rapa 的山脊上曾有十几个设防的村落，山上凿出了梯田和壕沟。如今，长老会仍在守护这片土地，rāhui 保护着礁石。","That’s a white tern. Look for something green.":"那是一只白燕鸥。找找绿色的东西。","Distance: {#1} m":"距离：{#1} m","Speed: {#1} knots":"速度：{#1} 节","You watched a mother and her calf, the way the guides of Rurutu do. In French Polynesia, all whales and dolphins are protected: inside {#1} m boats slow down and come alongside, they never chase, cut in front or come between a mother and calf, and only licensed operators may take swimmers in the water. The rules were made stricter in {#2}.":"你像 Rurutu 的向导那样，观赏了一头鲸妈妈和她的幼鲸。在法属波利尼西亚，所有鲸和海豚都受到保护：在 {#1} m 范围内，船只要减速并从侧面靠近，绝不追赶、绝不抢到前方，也绝不插到母鲸和幼鲸之间；只有持证经营者才能带游客下水。这些规定在 {#2} 年变得更加严格。","With a guide from Haurei you climb to Morongo Uta, a fort on the ridge built about {#1} years ago. <b>Which way?</b> ({#2} / {#3})":"你和一位来自 Haurei 的向导爬上 Morongo Uta，这是一座约 {#1} 年前建在山脊上的要塞。<b>走哪条路？</b>（{#2} / {#3}）","The basket you are weaving":"你正在编的篮子","The weaver asks for a strip of":"编织女工向你要一根叶条，颜色是","Pandanus strips are dyed in many colours. Tap the colour she names.":"露兜树叶条被染成许多颜色。点击她说的颜色。","Rows woven":"已编行数","{A}: {B}. One more row.":"{A}：{B}。再编一行。","Your ʻete is finished, woven in six colours. The weaver ties off the rim and smiles:":"你的 ʻete 编好了，用了六种颜色。编织女工收好篮口，笑着说：","Under a thatched shelter on Raivavae, a dugout hull on trestles and a new plank to sew on":"在 Raivavae 的一座茅草棚下，支架上架着一个挖凿而成的船体，旁边是一块要缝上去的新木板","Raivavae is the only island of French Polynesia where canoes are still <b>sewn</b>: a hull dug from one trunk, raised with planks tied on with cord. <b>{#1}. Shave the plank</b> with the adze until its edge sits flat on the hull. Hold, and release in the green zone.":"Raivavae 是法属波利尼西亚唯一一座至今仍在<b>缝制</b>独木舟的岛：船体由一整根树干挖成，再用绳子绑上木板加高。<b>{#1}. 刨削木板</b>，用锛子修到它的边缘能平贴在船体上。按住，在绿色区域松开。","<b>{#1}. Drill the holes</b> in pairs, one through the plank and one through the hull edge, with the bow drill. <b>Tap each orange ring.</b>":"<b>{#1}. 钻孔</b>，用弓钻成对地钻：一个穿过木板，一个穿过船体边缘。<b>点击每个橙色圆环。</b>","<b>{#1}. Lash, <span>nati</span>:</b> pass the coconut-fibre cord, <span>nape</span>, through each pair of holes and pull it tight, from bow to stern. <b>Tap the glowing ring</b> each time.":"<b>{#1}. 捆绑，<span>nati</span>：</b>把椰纤维绳 <span>nape</span> 穿过每一对孔并拉紧，从船头到船尾。每次都<b>点击发光的圆环</b>。","<b>{#1}. Seal the seam</b> so the sea stays out: press fibre and breadfruit gum along it. <b>Slide your finger along the seam</b>, from bow to stern.":"<b>{#1}. 密封接缝</b>，不让海水进来：沿着接缝压入纤维和面包果树胶。<b>用手指沿着接缝滑动</b>，从船头到船尾。","The new plank is sewn on and the seam is sealed. Time to see if it floats dry!":"新木板缝好了，接缝也密封好了。来看看它下水后会不会漏水吧！","Your sewn plank holds, and not a drop comes in. Before nails and screws, canoes across Polynesia were built this way: planks shaped with stone adzes and sewn on with sennit cord. Raivavae still keeps the skill alive.":"你缝上的木板很牢固，一滴水也没渗进来。在有钉子和螺丝之前，整个波利尼西亚的独木舟都是这样造的：用石锛削出木板，再用椰纤维绳缝上去。Raivavae 至今仍保留着这门手艺。","A clean pair of holes.":"一对干净利落的孔。","Start at the bow: the next pair is the glowing one.":"从船头开始：下一对是发光的那一对。","Pull it tight.":"拉紧。","All seven are lashed: the plank cannot move.":"七对都绑好了：木板纹丝不动。","Sealed from bow to stern.":"从船头到船尾都密封好了。","pink pūpū":"粉色 pūpū","yellow pūpū":"黄色 pūpū","brown dove shell":"棕色核螺","The white sand of motu Vaiamanu, the swimming-pool motu of Raivavae, with its turquoise basin":"Vaiamanu 小岛（motu）的白沙滩，Raivavae 的“游泳池小岛”，还有它碧绿的水池","On motu Vaiamanu, the “swimming-pool motu”, the women of Raivavae gather tiny shells for necklaces. <b>Pick up {#1} empty shells:</b> some are still somebody’s home.":"在 Vaiamanu 小岛，也就是“游泳池小岛”上，Raivavae 的女人们收集小贝壳来做项链。<b>捡起 {#1} 个空贝壳：</b>有些贝壳里还住着别人呢。","Pierce the shell":"给贝壳钻孔","The mama’s pattern":"妈妈的图案","… and again":"……再重复","Empty and shiny: a {A}.":"空的，还闪闪发亮：一个{A}。","Not this bowl: look at the colour.":"不是这个碗：看看颜色。","Sorted.":"分好了。","All pierced, none broken.":"全都钻好了孔，一个也没碎。","<b>{#1}. Sort them by colour</b> into the coconut bowls, as the mama does: it is a labour of patience. <b>Tap a shell, then its bowl.</b>":"<b>{#1}. 按颜色分类</b>，放进椰壳碗里，就像妈妈做的那样：这是一件考验耐心的活儿。<b>先点击一个贝壳，再点击它的碗。</b>","<b>{#1}. Pierce each shell</b> with a fine needle, gently: a tiny shell breaks easily. <b>Tap each one.</b>":"<b>{#1}. 给每个贝壳钻孔</b>，用细针轻轻地钻：小贝壳很容易碎。<b>点击每一个。</b>","<b>{#1}. String them</b> following the mama’s pattern: white cowry, pink, yellow, brown… and again.":"<b>{#1}. 把它们串起来</b>，按照妈妈的图案：白宝贝螺、粉色、黄色、棕色……再重复。","Tied with a knot of coconut fibre.":"用椰纤维打了个结系好。","Your hei pūpū is finished, and your manu wears it proudly. On Raivavae, the women gather tiny shells on the motu, sort them by colour for days, and string them into necklaces; they also weave hats and mats and sew tīfaifai quilts. Take only empty shells, and never living ones from the lagoon.":"你的 hei pūpū 做好了，你的 manu 骄傲地戴上了它。在 Raivavae，女人们在 motu 上收集小贝壳，花好几天按颜色分类，再串成项链；她们还编帽子、席子，缝 tīfaifai 拼布被。只捡空贝壳，绝不要从泻湖里拿走活的贝。","Green and flowering: the potatoes are still small.":"还绿着、正在开花：土豆还很小。","A firm, heavy head: cut it.":"菜球紧实又沉：割下来。","Loose leaves and no head yet: give it time.":"叶子松散，还没结球：再等等。","Rows of vegetables in the dark soil of Tubuai, under Mount Taitaʻa":"Taitaʻa 山下，Tubuai 深色泥土里的一排排蔬菜","Tubuai is cooler than Tahiti: potatoes, carrots, leeks and cabbages grow here, which is why it is called a granary of French Polynesia. <b>Harvest only what is ready</b>, and leave the rest to grow.":"Tubuai 比 Tahiti 凉爽：土豆、胡萝卜、韭葱和卷心菜都能在这里生长，所以它被称为法属波利尼西亚的粮仓。<b>只收获已经成熟的</b>，其余的留着继续长。","Your crates go to the airport and the cargo ship. Thanks to its cooler climate, Tubuai grows the vegetables of temperate lands, potatoes, carrots, leeks and cabbages, as well as taro: much of it is sold in Tahiti.":"你的木箱被送往机场和货轮。得益于较凉爽的气候，Tubuai 能种植温带地区的蔬菜，比如土豆、胡萝卜、韭葱和卷心菜，还有芋头：大部分都销往 Tahiti。","The marae Hariitaʻata of Tubuai: a paved court edged with upright basalt slabs, among taro fields under Mount Taitaʻa":"Tubuai 的 marae Hariitaʻata：一座铺石的庭院，四周围着直立的玄武岩石板，坐落在 Taitaʻa 山下的芋头田之间","With the heritage team you restore <b>marae Hariitaʻata</b>, at Tamatoa among the taro fields. Roots have crept into the paving and three slabs have fallen. <b>{#1}. Dig out the roots:</b> tap each one.":"你和文化遗产团队一起修复 <b>marae Hariitaʻata</b>，它位于 Tamatoa 的芋头田之间。树根钻进了铺石，三块石板倒了。<b>{#1}. 挖出树根：</b>点击每一条。","<b>{#1}. Raise the fallen slabs.</b> Marae of the Australs are edged with upright stones. <b>Tap a fallen slab, then the gap where it stood.</b>":"<b>{#1}. 扶起倒下的石板。</b>南方群岛的 marae 四周都围着立石。<b>先点击一块倒下的石板，再点击它原来所在的缺口。</b>","<b>{#1}. Re-lay the paving.</b> Three stones are missing from the court. <b>Tap a stone, then the gap that matches its shape.</b>":"<b>{#1}. 重新铺石。</b>庭院里少了三块石头。<b>先点击一块石头，再点击和它形状相符的缺口。</b>","<b>{#1}. Something under the grass.</b> Where the roots were, the ground is dark and soft. <b>Tap it</b> to brush it clean.":"<b>{#1}. 草下有东西。</b>树根原来所在的地方，地面又黑又软。<b>点击它</b>，把它刷干净。","Out, root and all.":"连根拔出来了。","It stands again.":"它重新立起来了。","All three stand. The court has its edge back.":"三块都立起来了。庭院又有了它的边界。","Not that gap: look at the size of the slab.":"不是那个缺口：看看石板的大小。","Not that gap: match the shape.":"不是那个缺口：要形状相符。","A cooking pit!":"一个烹煮坑！","Blackened stones and charcoal: the restorers of Hariitaʻata found an older paving and a pit like this one under the marae.":"熏黑的石头和木炭：修复 Hariitaʻata 的人在 marae 下面发现了更古老的铺石和一个像这样的坑。","You helped put marae Hariitaʻata back together: roots dug out, slabs raised, paving re-laid, and an old cooking pit uncovered. On Tubuai, the marae were places of the chiefs’ councils and of ceremonies; the Direction de la culture et du patrimoine restored this one with the people of the island. Visit marae with a guide, and never climb on them or take a stone.":"你帮忙把 marae Hariitaʻata 重新修好了：挖出了树根，扶起了石板，重新铺好了石头，还发现了一个古老的烹煮坑。在 Tubuai，marae 曾是酋长议事和举行仪式的地方；文化与遗产局（Direction de la culture et du patrimoine）和岛上居民一起修复了这一座。参观 marae 要跟着向导，绝不要爬上去或拿走石头。","The children’s stone":"儿童石","The women’s stone, about {#1} kg":"女子石，约 {#1} 公斤","On the village green of Moerai, at the end of the Tere, a tall basalt stone waits to be lifted; the crowd and an orator watch":"在 Moerai 村的草坪上，Tere 环岛之行的终点，一块高高的玄武岩石等着被举起；人群和一位演说者在一旁观看","Every January the three villages of Rurutu, Moerai, Avera and Hauti, go around their island together: the <b>Tere</b>. At each stop the <span>ʻōrero</span> recites the history of the place. Then the strong lift each village’s stones: the <b>amoraʻa ʻōfaʻi</b>. The stones are tall pillars of basalt. Which one will your manu try?":"每年一月，Rurutu 的三个村庄 Moerai、Avera 和 Hauti 一起环绕全岛而行：这就是 <b>Tere</b>。每到一站，<span>ʻōrero</span> 都会讲述当地的历史。然后，大力士们举起每个村庄的石头：这就是 <b>amoraʻa ʻōfaʻi</b>。这些石头是高高的玄武岩石柱。你的 manu 要试哪一块呢？","The crowd laughs kindly: only the strongest lift that one, and the record is over {#1} kg. Your manu hugs it… it does not move! Take the children’s stone.":"人群善意地笑了：只有最强壮的人才能举起那块，纪录超过 {#1} 公斤。你的 manu 抱住它……它纹丝不动！还是选儿童石吧。","The women of Rurutu lift this one, about {#1} kg. Your manu pulls… not a centimetre. The children’s stone, then!":"Rurutu 的女子举的就是这块，约 {#1} 公斤。你的 manu 用力一拉……一厘米也没动。那就选儿童石吧！","In the old days the stone was rubbed with <b>monoʻi</b> to make it slippery and the lift harder. Today it is often bare. Do you want the true old way?":"从前，人们会在石头上抹 <b>monoʻi</b>，让它变滑，举起来更难。如今石头常常不抹油。你想试试真正的古老方式吗？","Rub it with monoʻi":"抹上 monoʻi","Leave it bare":"不抹油","{#1}. Squat deep and hug the stone":"{#1}. 深深蹲下，把石头","to your chest, barefoot, in your pāreu. Hold, and release when your grip is in the green zone: with monoʻi the zone is narrow!":"紧紧抱在胸前，赤着脚，穿着 pāreu。按住不放，当握力进入绿色区域时松开：抹了 monoʻi，绿色区域会很窄！","to your chest, barefoot, in your pāreu. Hold, and release when your grip is in the green zone.":"紧紧抱在胸前，赤着脚，穿着 pāreu。按住不放，当握力进入绿色区域时松开。","Hold to squat and hug":"按住以蹲下抱石","Not low enough: hug it closer, knees bent.":"蹲得不够低：膝盖弯曲，抱得再紧一点。","Too long in the squat: your legs are shaking. Stand, breathe, and try again.":"蹲得太久了：你的腿在发抖。站起来，深呼吸，再试一次。","<b>{#1}. Lift on the beat of the pahu:</b> tap <b>Lift!</b> when the red ring meets the black one: to the thigh, to the chest, onto the shoulder. Off the beat, the stone slips down a step.":"<b>{#1}. 跟着 pahu 鼓的节拍举起：</b>当红圈与黑圈重合时点击 <b>举起！</b>：举到大腿，举到胸前，再扛上肩膀。没踩准节拍，石头就会往下滑一级。","To the thigh!":"举到大腿！","To the chest!":"举到胸前！","Off the beat, and the monoʻi makes it slide: it slips down a step.":"没踩准节拍，monoʻi 又让石头打滑：它往下滑了一级。","Off the beat: the stone slips down a step. Wait for the rings to meet.":"没踩准节拍：石头往下滑了一级。等两个圆圈重合再点。","<b>{#1}. Balance it on the shoulder</b>, then the referee waits for your other hand to let go. Keep the dot in the green: tap <b>Lean left</b> or <b>Lean right</b> for two seconds.":"<b>{#1}. 把石头稳稳扛在肩上</b>，然后裁判会等你的另一只手松开。让圆点保持在绿色区域：点击 <b>向左倾</b> 或 <b>向右倾</b>，坚持两秒。","The other hand lets go:":"另一只手松开了：","good lift!":"举得好！","Your manu lifted the oiled stone onto its shoulder after a few slips, the old way, and the Tere cheers. On Rurutu the island tour of January ends with the amoraʻa ʻōfaʻi: tall basalt stones, about {#1} kg for the women and {#2} kg for the men, hugged from a deep squat and raised onto the shoulder.":"你的 manu 滑了几次之后，按古老的方式把抹了油的石头扛上了肩膀，Tere 的人群欢呼起来。在 Rurutu，一月的环岛之行以 amoraʻa ʻōfaʻi 收尾：高高的玄武岩石，女子举的约 {#1} 公斤，男子举的约 {#2} 公斤，从深蹲姿势抱起，再扛上肩膀。","Your manu lifted the stone onto its shoulder after a few slips, and the Tere cheers. On Rurutu the island tour of January ends with the amoraʻa ʻōfaʻi: tall basalt stones, about {#1} kg for the women and {#2} kg for the men, hugged from a deep squat and raised onto the shoulder.":"你的 manu 滑了几次之后，把石头扛上了肩膀，Tere 的人群欢呼起来。在 Rurutu，一月的环岛之行以 amoraʻa ʻōfaʻi 收尾：高高的玄武岩石，女子举的约 {#1} 公斤，男子举的约 {#2} 公斤，从深蹲姿势抱起，再扛上肩膀。","Your manu lifted the oiled stone onto its shoulder on the first try, the old way, and the Tere cheers. On Rurutu the island tour of January ends with the amoraʻa ʻōfaʻi: tall basalt stones, about {#1} kg for the women and {#2} kg for the men, hugged from a deep squat and raised onto the shoulder.":"你的 manu 第一次就按古老的方式把抹了油的石头扛上了肩膀，Tere 的人群欢呼起来。在 Rurutu，一月的环岛之行以 amoraʻa ʻōfaʻi 收尾：高高的玄武岩石，女子举的约 {#1} 公斤，男子举的约 {#2} 公斤，从深蹲姿势抱起，再扛上肩膀。","Your manu lifted the stone onto its shoulder on the first try, and the Tere cheers. On Rurutu the island tour of January ends with the amoraʻa ʻōfaʻi: tall basalt stones, about {#1} kg for the women and {#2} kg for the men, hugged from a deep squat and raised onto the shoulder.":"你的 manu 第一次就把石头扛上了肩膀，Tere 的人群欢呼起来。在 Rurutu，一月的环岛之行以 amoraʻa ʻōfaʻi 收尾：高高的玄武岩石，女子举的约 {#1} 公斤，男子举的约 {#2} 公斤，从深蹲姿势抱起，再扛上肩膀。","It tips over: back to the chest. On the beat, onto the shoulder again!":"石头歪倒了：退回到胸前。跟着节拍，再扛上肩膀！","A drop of water hangs at its tip. Each drop leaves a tiny ring of calcite: a stalactite grows only a few millimetres in a human life. The formations of Rurutu are about {#1} years old.":"一滴水挂在它的尖端。每一滴水都会留下一圈细小的方解石：一根钟乳石在人的一生中只能长几毫米。Rurutu 的这些钟乳石形成物已有约 {#1} 年历史。","The monster’s teeth":"怪兽的牙齿","Where a stalactite from the roof meets a stalagmite from the floor, a column forms. Rows of them look like the teeth of a great mouth: the people of Rurutu call these caves “the monster”.":"从洞顶垂下的钟乳石与从地面长起的石笋相接，便形成了石柱。一排排石柱就像一张巨口里的牙齿：Rurutu 的人们把这些洞穴叫作“怪兽”。","Rimstone pools":"边石池","Water running over the floor leaves little walls of calcite that hold pools: gours. In Toarutu, “the monster of Rurutu”, they are full of clear water. Never step in them: the rims break.":"流过地面的水留下一道道方解石矮墙，围成一个个水池：这就是边石池。在 Toarutu，也就是“Rurutu 的怪兽”里，池中满是清澈的水。千万不要踩进去：池边会碎。","Shells in the wall":"岩壁里的贝壳","Rurutu’s cliffs are an old coral reef pushed up from the sea, the makatea. In the cave of Tupumai the walls are set with shells that lived in that reef long ago.":"Rurutu 的悬崖是从海中抬升起来的古老珊瑚礁，叫作 makatea。在 Tupumai 洞里，岩壁上嵌满了很久以前生活在那片礁石中的贝壳。","An old earth oven":"古老的地炉","At the back of Ana Aeo, the Mitterrand cave, a pit about {#1} m wide was an umu, an earth oven. People once sheltered and cooked in these caves; some were burial places, so visit only with a guide.":"在 Ana Aeo（密特朗洞）的深处，有一个宽约 {#1} 米的坑，那曾是一座 umu，也就是地炉。人们曾在这些洞穴里躲避风雨、烹煮食物；有些洞穴是墓葬之地，所以只能跟着向导参观。","A tropicbird at the entrance":"洞口的鹲鸟","A white tropicbird, its long tail streamers trailing, nests in a hollow of the cliff by the entrance. Pass quietly: they nest here in June.":"一只白色的鹲鸟拖着长长的尾羽，在洞口旁悬崖的一个凹洞里筑巢。请安静地经过：它们六月在这里筑巢。","Inside a limestone cave of Rurutu, lit by a torch: stalactites, columns, rimstone pools and an old earth oven":"在 Rurutu 的一个石灰岩洞穴里，火把照亮了钟乳石、石柱、边石池和一座古老的地炉","With a guide from Moerai you enter the caves in the makatea, the raised coral cliff of Rurutu. <b>Drag the torch</b> around the cave and <b>tap what you find</b>: six things. Look, but never touch or break anything.":"跟着一位来自 Moerai 的向导，你走进 makatea（Rurutu 隆起的珊瑚悬崖）中的洞穴。<b>拖动火把</b>照遍洞穴，<b>点击你发现的东西</b>：一共六样。只看，千万不要触摸或弄坏任何东西。","Your manu spots a little broken stalactite on the floor, as long as a finger, and would like to keep it as a souvenir…":"你的 manu 发现地上有一小截断掉的钟乳石，有一根手指那么长，很想把它留作纪念……","You explored the caves of Rurutu with your torch and left them as you found them. Rurutu is a raised island: its old coral reef rose out of the sea and became cliffs full of caves, the ana, about thirty of them. Some were shelters, others burial places: go only with a guide.":"你举着火把探索了 Rurutu 的洞穴，离开时让它们保持原样。Rurutu 是一座隆起岛：古老的珊瑚礁从海中升起，变成了布满洞穴的悬崖，这些洞穴叫作 ana，大约有三十个。有些曾是避难所，有些是墓葬之地：一定要跟着向导去。","Seen from above off the coast of Rurutu: a humpback whale and her calf resting beyond the reef, and the guide’s small boat":"从 Rurutu 海岸外的空中俯瞰：一头座头鲸和她的幼鲸在礁石外休息，旁边是向导的小船","July to October: humpback whales, up to {#1} m and {#2} tonnes, come from the Antarctic to give birth off Rurutu. The reef is close to the shore, so they rest in the bays. You go out with a licensed guide. <b>How do you approach the mother and her calf?</b>":"七月到十月，体长可达 {#1} 米、体重可达 {#2} 吨的座头鲸从南极来到 Rurutu 附近海域产仔。这里的礁石离岸很近，所以它们会在海湾里休息。你跟着一位持证向导出海。<b>你要怎样接近鲸妈妈和她的幼鲸？</b>","Look under the surface":"看看水下","<b>Engine off.</b> You drift quietly. A blow rises like a puff of smoke: the calf breathes. Your guide hands you a mask to look over the side.":"<b>关掉引擎。</b>你静静地漂着。一股喷气像一缕烟一样升起：那是幼鲸在呼吸。向导递给你一副面镜，让你从船边往下看。","Under the surface, the mother rests, still, ten metres down, her long white flippers spread. The calf rises to breathe every few minutes, then glides back down to her. You only watch from the boat.":"水面下，鲸妈妈在十米深处静静休息，长长的白色胸鳍舒展开来。幼鲸每隔几分钟就浮上来呼吸，然后又滑回她身边。你只在船上观看。","You watched a mother and her calf, the way the guides of Rurutu do. In French Polynesia, all whales and dolphins are protected: inside {#1} m boats slow down and come alongside, they never chase, cut in front or come between a mother and calf, and only licensed operators may take swimmers in the water.":"你像 Rurutu 的向导们那样，观看了一对鲸妈妈和幼鲸。在法属波利尼西亚，所有鲸和海豚都受到保护：在 {#1} 米范围内，船只要减速，从侧面靠近；绝不追逐、绝不抢到它们前方，也绝不插到母鲸和幼鲸之间；只有持证经营者才能带游客下水。","You watched a mother and her calf without a single mistake, the way the guides of Rurutu do. In French Polynesia, all whales and dolphins are protected: inside {#1} m boats slow down and come alongside, they never chase, cut in front or come between a mother and calf, and only licensed operators may take swimmers in the water.":"你像 Rurutu 的向导们那样，一次失误都没有，观看了一对鲸妈妈和幼鲸。在法属波利尼西亚，所有鲸和海豚都受到保护：在 {#1} 米范围内，船只要减速，从侧面靠近；绝不追逐、绝不抢到它们前方，也绝不插到母鲸和幼鲸之间；只有持证经营者才能带游客下水。","A garden of Rimatara by the sea: coconut palms in flower, a banana plant with its hanging purple flower, a red hibiscus and a little church; birds come to drink nectar":"海边的一座 Rimatara 花园：开花的椰子树、垂着紫色花苞的香蕉树、一株红色木槿和一座小教堂；鸟儿飞来吸食花蜜","With a guide from Amaru you watch the trees. The <span>ʻura</span> drinks nectar from coconut and banana flowers. <b>Tap a bird</b> to raise the binoculars, then say which bird it is. Find <b>five ʻura</b>: red cheeks and breast, green back, a blue nape.":"你跟着一位来自 Amaru 的向导观察树丛。<span>ʻura</span> 吸食椰子花和香蕉花的花蜜。<b>点击一只鸟</b>举起双筒望远镜，然后说出它是哪种鸟。找到<b>五只 ʻura</b>：红色的脸颊和胸口，绿色的背，蓝色的后颈。","Look again: red cheeks and breast, a green back and a blue nape. That is an ʻura!":"再看看：红色的脸颊和胸口，绿色的背，蓝色的后颈。那是 ʻura！","Look again: a brown body, a black head and a yellow patch round the eye. That is a myna.":"再看看：棕色的身体，黑色的头，眼睛周围一圈黄斑。那是家八哥。","Look again: plain olive-brown, pale yellow below, a long thin bill. That is the reed warbler.":"再看看：一身朴素的橄榄褐色，腹部淡黄，喙又细又长。那是苇莺。","There it is, its brush tongue in the flower.":"在那儿，它正把刷子般的舌头伸进花里。","Another ʻura, quick and noisy.":"又一只 ʻura，又快又吵。","Yes: the blue nape, the red cheeks.":"对：蓝色的后颈，红色的脸颊。","Right, a common myna, brought from Asia. It takes the tree holes where the ʻura would nest.":"对，这是从亚洲引进的家八哥。它会占据 ʻura 本来要筑巢的树洞。","Right, the Rimatara reed warbler: it too lives only on this island, in the reeds and the bush.":"对，这是里马塔拉苇莺：它也只生活在这座岛上，栖息在芦苇和灌木丛中。","Yes. A royal tapu has protected the ʻura since about {#1}. It may not be caught, hurt or taken away.":"对。大约从 {#1} 年起，一道王室的 tapu 就一直保护着 ʻura。不能捕捉、伤害或带走它。","Rapa: jagged green ridges in the mist above Ahurei bay, and flooded taro fields with stone banks":"Rapa：Ahurei 湾上方雾中参差的绿色山脊，以及用石堤围起的芋头水田","On Rapa, taro grows in flooded fields held by stone banks, and becomes <span>pōpoi</span>, the island’s staple. <b>{#1}. Pull up the ripe taro</b>: their leaves are turning yellow.":"在 Rapa，芋头长在由石堤围住的水田里，并被做成 <span>pōpoi</span>，这是岛上的主食。<b>{#1}. 拔出成熟的芋头</b>：它们的叶子正在变黄。","Five taro in the basket. <b>And the leafy tops you cut off?</b>":"篮子里有五个芋头了。<b>那切下来的带叶顶部呢？</b>","Replant them in the mud: they will grow new taro":"把它们重新种回泥里：会长出新的芋头","Feed them to the pigs":"拿去喂猪","Yes: the top of each corm is pushed back into the mud, and the field goes on.":"对：每个芋头球茎的顶部都被插回泥里，水田就这样延续下去。","The tops are kept: they are how taro is planted again.":"顶部要留着：芋头就是靠它们重新种下的。","Hot stones":"烧热的石头","The taro":"芋头","Banana and tī leaves":"香蕉叶和 tī（朱蕉）叶","Earth to close it":"盖上泥土封好","<b>{#1}. Cook the taro in the earth oven.</b> Build it in the right order, from the bottom up.":"<b>{#1}. 用土灶烤芋头。</b>按正确的顺序从下往上搭好。","First the stones, heated red in a fire.":"先放石头，在火里烧得通红。","Now the taro, right on the hot stones.":"现在放芋头，直接放在热石头上。","Cover the taro with leaves first, or the earth gets in.":"先用叶子盖住芋头，否则泥土会掉进去。","Closed. Now the steam cooks the taro for hours.":"封好了。现在蒸汽会把芋头焖上好几个小时。","<b>{#1}. Peel</b> the cooked taro while it is warm: <b>tap each corm</b>. The flesh of Rapa’s taro is a soft lilac-grey.":"<b>{#1}. 剥皮</b>：趁煮熟的芋头还温热时剥去外皮：<b>点击每个球茎</b>。Rapa 芋头的果肉是柔和的淡紫灰色。","<b>{#1}. Pound it</b> on the wooden board with the stone <span>penu</span>. <b>Tap Pound</b> when the drum ring closes. When the paste grows stiff and cracks, wet your hands with a little water.":"<b>{#1}. 捶打</b>：在木板上用石杵 <span>penu</span> 捶。<b>当鼓圈合拢时点击“捶打”</b>。当芋泥变硬开裂时，用一点水沾湿双手。","Wet your hands":"沾湿双手","Too stiff: the penu bounces off. Wet your hands.":"太硬了：penu 被弹开了。沾湿双手吧。","Good blow: a lump flattens.":"捶得好：一个面团被压平了。","Off the beat: tiring, and the lumps stay. Strike when the ring closes.":"没踩准节拍：又累，面团还在。等鼓圈合拢时再捶。","Wet hands: the paste turns soft again.":"双手沾湿了：芋泥又变软了。","<b>{#1}. Wrap it</b> in the long leaves of the <b>tī</b> plant, then tie it. <b>Tap Fold a leaf</b> four times.":"<b>{#1}. 包起来</b>：用 <b>tī</b> 植物的长叶子包好，然后扎紧。<b>点击“折叶子”</b>四次。","Fold a leaf":"折叶子","<b>{#1}. Let it sour</b> for a few days in the cool of the house. Sour pōpoi keeps a long time: food for the cold months, and for long voyages.":"<b>{#1}. 让它发酸</b>，在屋里阴凉处放几天。发酸的 pōpoi 能保存很久：是寒冷月份的食物，也是远航的干粮。","Up it comes, muddy and heavy.":"拔出来了，沾满泥，沉甸甸的。","A fine corm.":"一个很棒的球茎。","Your pōpoi is ready: smooth, a little sour, and it keeps for a long time. Rapa once had about twenty times more taro fields than today, and they fed the whole island; stone pounders by the dozen were found in its old hill forts. Families still work the fields together and give you a bundle of pōpoi for your canoe.":"你的 pōpoi 做好了：细腻、微酸，能保存很久。Rapa 的芋头水田曾经是今天的大约二十倍，养活了全岛的人；在古老的山顶要塞里发现过成打的石杵。如今各家仍一起耕种水田，还送给你一包 pōpoi 带上独木舟。","The ridge of Rapa above Haʻurei bay, with the hill fort of Morongo Uta on the summit: a stone-faced tower, terraces and ditches cut across the ridge":"Haʻurei 湾上方的 Rapa 山脊，山顶上是 Morongo Uta 山顶要塞：一座石砌的塔台、台地，以及横切山脊的壕沟","With a guide from Haʻurei you climb to <b>Morongo Uta</b>, the oldest of Rapa’s hill forts, on the ridge 258 m above the bay. <b>Which way?</b> ({A} / 6)":"你跟着一位来自 Haʻurei 的向导爬上 <b>Morongo Uta</b>，这是 Rapa 最古老的山顶要塞，位于海湾上方 258 m 的山脊上。<b>往哪边走？</b>（{A} / 6）","Climb the old stone wall of a terrace":"爬上一处台地的古老石墙","The highest peak was cut flat and faced with stone. Its top, about {#1} by {#2} metres, held a stone-lined oven. From here the lookouts watched the bays.":"最高的山峰被削平并砌上石块。它的顶部大约 {#1} × {#2} 米，上面有一个石砌的灶。瞭望者在这里守望各个海湾。","A house terrace":"一处房屋台地","{#1} terraces step down the ridge. Houses of wood and leaves stood on them, with a hearth of three or four flat stones. Perhaps {#2} people lived here, between about {#3} and {#4}.":"{#1} 层台地沿山脊层层而下。上面曾建有木头和树叶搭成的房屋，屋里有用三四块扁平石头围成的炉灶。大约在 {#3} 年到 {#4} 年之间，这里也许住着 {#2} 人。","A fosse":"一道壕沟","This ditch was dug across the ridge to stop attackers. Wooden palisades once stood above it.":"这条壕沟横挖过山脊，用来阻挡进攻者。上面曾经立着木栅栏。","You stand on the fort. <b>Tap the four glowing places</b> to learn what you see.":"你站在要塞上。<b>点击四个发光的地方</b>，了解你看到的东西。","In the grass lies a stone <b>pounder</b>, a penu, like the {#1} found here in {#2}. Your manu would like to keep it…":"草丛里躺着一个石<b>杵</b>，也就是 penu，就像 {#2} 年在这里发现的 {#1} 个一样。你的 manu 很想把它留下……","Leave it where it lies":"让它留在原处","Take it home":"带回家","Right: what belongs to the site stays at the site, for the people of Rapa and the archaeologists.":"对：属于遗址的东西就留在遗址，留给 Rapa 的人们和考古学家。","No: taking anything from a site is forbidden, and it would lose its story.":"不行：从遗址拿走任何东西都是禁止的，而且它会失去自己的故事。","You climbed to Morongo Uta, explored its tower, terraces and fosses, left the pounder where it lay, saw the koko and respected the rāhui. Rapa has fourteen hill forts on its ridges, built from about {#1}, when the island’s taro fields fed some two thousand people. Today a council of elders still looks after the land, and rāhui protect the reefs.":"你爬上了 Morongo Uta，探索了它的塔台、台地和壕沟，把石杵留在了原处，看到了 koko，也遵守了 rāhui。Rapa 的山脊上共有十四座山顶要塞，大约从 {#1} 年开始修建，那时岛上的芋头水田养活了约两千人。如今仍有一个长老会照管这片土地，rāhui 也保护着礁石。","A wild goat. Goats and fires have eaten much of Rapa’s forest: that is why the koko is so rare. Look for something green in the trees.":"一只野山羊。山羊和火灾吞噬了 Rapa 的大片森林：这就是 koko 如此稀少的原因。在树丛里找找绿色的东西吧。","That’s a white tern. Look for a green dove in the forest below.":"那是一只白燕鸥。到下面的森林里找一只绿色的鸽子吧。","You crouch low and hold the grass: the gust passes over you.":"你蹲低身子抓住草丛：阵风从你头上掠过。","Gust! Crouch and hold on":"阵风！蹲下抓牢","A gust of wind rushes up the ridge!":"一阵大风沿着山脊冲上来！","The gust pushes you back down the path. On Rapa’s ridges, crouch when the wind comes!":"阵风把你推回了山路下方。在 Rapa 的山脊上，起风时要蹲下！","You cross a <b>fosse</b>, a deep ditch cut across the ridge: enemies could only come one at a time, under the palisade.":"你穿过一道<b>壕沟</b>，一条横切山脊的深沟：敌人只能一个接一个地过来，暴露在栅栏之下。","The <b>koko</b>! The Rapa fruit dove: a blue-grey head with a pink crown, a rose band on the chest, a yellow belly. Found only on Rapa: about {#1} were counted in {#2}.":"<b>koko</b>！拉帕果鸠：蓝灰色的头，粉红色的头顶，胸前一道玫瑰色的带，黄色的腹部。只生活在 Rapa：{#2} 年统计到大约 {#1} 只。","Now look down at the forest on the slope: something moves in the trees… <b>can you find the <span>koko</span></b>, the Rapa fruit dove?":"现在往下看山坡上的森林：树丛里有东西在动……<b>你能找到 <span>koko</span></b>，也就是拉帕果鸠吗？","You found five ʻura. Rimatara has no black rats, which eat eggs and chicks, so the lorikeet lives on here while it vanished from the other islands. Queen Tamaeva V declared it tapu around {#1}, and in {#2} some birds were taken to Atiu in the Cook Islands, with Rimatara’s agreement: there are now more than {#3}.":"你找到了五只 ʻura。Rimatara 没有会吃鸟蛋和雏鸟的黑家鼠，所以当这种吸蜜鹦鹉在其他岛屿消失时，它仍在这里生存。大约 {#1} 年，Tamaeva V 女王宣布它为 tapu；{#2} 年，经 Rimatara 同意，一些鸟被带到了库克群岛的 Atiu 岛：如今那里已有超过 {#3} 只。","You found five ʻura without a single mistake. Rimatara has no black rats, which eat eggs and chicks, so the lorikeet lives on here while it vanished from the other islands. Queen Tamaeva V declared it tapu around {#1}, and in {#2} some birds were taken to Atiu in the Cook Islands, with Rimatara’s agreement: there are now more than {#3}.":"你一次都没出错就找到了五只 ʻura。Rimatara 没有会吃鸟蛋和雏鸟的黑家鼠，所以当这种吸蜜鹦鹉在其他岛屿消失时，它仍在这里生存。大约 {#1} 年，Tamaeva V 女王宣布它为 tapu；{#2} 年，经 Rimatara 同意，一些鸟被带到了库克群岛的 Atiu 岛：如今那里已有超过 {#3} 只。","<b>{#1}.</b> After the mutiny on the <b>Bounty</b>, Fletcher Christian looks for an island to hide on and chooses <b>Tubuai</b> from the charts. The first landing goes badly: a fight in the lagoon, twelve islanders killed, at the place still called <b>Bloody Bay</b>. The mutineers sail to Tahiti and come back in June with pigs, goats, plants and Tahitian friends. What do they do first?":"<b>{#1}.</b> <b>Bounty</b> 号哗变之后，Fletcher Christian 寻找一座可以藏身的岛，从海图上选中了 <b>Tubuai</b>。第一次登岸很不顺利：泻湖里发生了一场打斗，十二名岛民丧生，那个地方至今仍叫<b>血湾</b>。叛变者驶往 Tahiti，六月带着猪、山羊、植物和塔希提朋友回来。他们首先做什么？","A British ship came and arrested them":"一艘英国船来把他们抓走了","A cyclone destroyed the fort":"一场气旋摧毁了堡垒","A museum keeps things; the tiki were made for this island.":"博物馆只是保管东西；而这些 tiki 是为这座岛而造的。","A roll of white pandanus, <b>pipita</b>, ready for the weavers. For the finest white strips, the mamas boil the green leaves with lemon before the sun. Rimatara sells its rolls to weavers of all the islands; its neighbour Rurutu makes the hats.":"一卷白色的露兜树叶，<b>pipita</b>，可以交给编织者了。要得到最细最白的叶条，妈妈们会在晒太阳之前，把绿叶和柠檬一起煮。Rimatara 把它的叶卷卖给各岛的编织者；邻岛 Rurutu 则做帽子。","A round face, a quiet smile: the tiki of Raivavae.":"圆圆的脸，安静的微笑：这就是 Raivavae 的 tiki。","A wooden fort of about a hundred metres a side, with a moat fed by the lagoon and a drawbridge: Fort George, for King George.":"一座每边约一百米的木堡垒，壕沟引入泻湖的水，还有一座吊桥：Fort George，以 King George 之名。","Build a fort with a moat, on the land of chief Tamatoa":"建一座带壕沟的堡垒，在酋长 Tamatoa 的土地上","Chief Tamatoa":"酋长 Tamatoa","Cut the long leaves and clean them":"割下长叶并清理干净","Draw a blade along the leaf before weaving":"编织前用刀片沿叶子划一道","Dry them in the sun for several weeks":"在太阳下晒几个星期","First the leaves must be cut.":"得先把叶子割下来。","In the Louvre":"在卢浮宫","In the garden of the Gauguin museum at Papeari, Tahiti":"在 Tahiti 的 Papeari，Gauguin 博物馆的花园里","It hides among the bushes by the road. <b>Part the leaves</b> until you find it.":"它藏在路边的灌木丛中。<b>拨开树叶</b>，直到找到它。","King George the Third":"King George 三世","No pearls in the Australs.":"南方群岛没有珍珠。","No, they never left Polynesia.":"不，他们从没离开过波利尼西亚。","No: that is not what happened.":"不对：事情不是这样发生的。","Not there. Ask in the next village.":"不在那里。到下一个村子去问问。","Nothing but leaves.":"只有树叶。","On the marae of the island":"在岛上的 marae 上","One side after the other, round the square.":"一边接着一边，绕着正方形。","Only the small one stayed.":"只有那尊小的留下了。","Plant gardens and ask the chiefs for land":"开辟菜园，向酋长们要土地","Pull out the central rib":"抽掉中间的叶脉","Raise the palisade, <b>one side after the other</b>, around the square.":"<b>一边接着一边</b>，绕着正方形立起栅栏。","Raivavae once had <b>four great stone tiki</b>, taller than a man. In {#1} three were taken to Tahiti: two stand today in the garden of the Gauguin museum at Papeari, the third sank while it was being loaded. One small tiki stayed on the island, a <b>smiling tiki</b> about a metre high. In which village does it stand?":"Raivavae 曾有<b>四尊巨大的石 tiki</b>，比人还高。{#1} 年，三尊被运到了 Tahiti：两尊今天立在 Papeari 的 Gauguin 博物馆花园里，第三尊在装船时沉入海中。一尊小 tiki 留在了岛上，一尊约一米高的<b>微笑 tiki</b>。它立在哪个村子？","Rimatara grows <b>paeʻore</b>, a pandanus without thorns, with leaves up to two metres long, and prepares it for the weavers of the whole territory. <b>Step {A} of {B}</b>: what comes next?":"Rimatara 种植 <b>paeʻore</b>，一种没有刺的露兜树，叶子长达两米，并把它加工好供全领地的编织者使用。<b>第 {A} 步，共 {B} 步</b>：接下来是什么？","Roll about eighty leaves into a tight roll":"把大约八十片叶子紧紧卷成一卷","She declared a tapu to protect the ʻura, the red lorikeet":"她宣布了一项 tapu，保护红色吸蜜鹦鹉 ʻura","She opened the first airstrip":"她开通了第一个机场","She started black pearl farming":"她开创了黑珍珠养殖","Soften each leaf by rolling it round the hands":"把每片叶子在手上绕着揉软","That is what the island asks for: its ancestors back, kept by their own people.":"这正是岛上所要求的：让祖先回家，由自己的人来看护。","The airstrip came in {#1}.":"机场是 {#1} 年建的。","The chief whose land they took.":"他们夺走了土地的那位酋长。","The islanders refused to give women and food; raids and battles followed, and the mutineers fell out among themselves":"岛民拒绝提供女人和食物；接着是袭击和战斗，叛变者之间也闹翻了","The islanders say that several of the men who moved the tiki in {#1} died strangely, and they still ask for the great tiki to <b>come home</b>. The museum answers that they could return if the island can keep them safe. What do you think?":"岛民说，{#1} 年搬运 tiki 的几个人后来死得蹊跷，他们至今仍要求大 tiki <b>回家</b>。博物馆回答说，只要岛上能妥善保护它们，它们就可以回去。你怎么看？","The man they had just put off the ship? No.":"他们刚把他赶下船的那个人？不对。","The mutineers named their fort on Tubuai after…":"叛变者在 Tubuai 的堡垒是以谁命名的……","They belong to Raivavae; a shelter and a guardian would bring them home":"它们属于 Raivavae；有一个遮棚和一位看护人，就能让它们回家","They belong to the museum now":"它们现在属于博物馆","They cannot be rolled while green: dry them first.":"绿叶没法卷：先晒干。","They were sailors on the run, not farmers: a fort first.":"他们是逃亡的水手，不是农民：先建堡垒。","Three months later the colony falls apart. <b>Why?</b>":"三个月后，殖民地瓦解了。<b>为什么？</b>","Today <b>nothing of the fort remains</b>: a quiet field by the lagoon at Taʻahuaia, on private land, with an orientation table of the old chiefdoms and a small museum room kept by an association of the island. The people of Tubuai remember the three bloody months of {#1} as their own story, not only the mutineers'.":"今天<b>堡垒什么也没剩下</b>：Taʻahuaia 泻湖边一片安静的田地，在私人土地上，有一张标出旧酋长领地的方位图，还有一个由岛上协会照看的小博物馆展室。Tubuai 的人们把 {#1} 年那血腥的三个月当作自己的故事来铭记，而不只是叛变者的故事。","What did Queen Tamaeva V of Rimatara do in {#1}?":"Rimatara 的女王 Tamaeva 五世在 {#1} 年做了什么？","Where are most of the great tiki of Raivavae today?":"Raivavae 的大 tiki 今天大多在哪里？","Yes, near Mahanatoa, by the road around the island.":"对，在 Mahanatoa 附近，环岛公路旁。","Yes. A battle killed sixty-six Tubuaians. In September the Bounty left: sixteen men stayed at Tahiti, Christian and eight others sailed on to Pitcairn.":"对。一场战斗夺去了六十六名 Tubuai 人的生命。九月，Bounty 号离开了：十六人留在 Tahiti，Christian 和另外八人继续航行到 Pitcairn。","Yes: Fort George. A strange loyalty, for mutineers.":"对：Fort George。对叛变者来说，这是一种奇怪的忠诚。","Yes: a square fort at Natiʻeva, today Taʻahuaia, on the north-east shore.":"对：一座方形堡垒，在 Natiʻeva，也就是今天的 Taʻahuaia，在东北岸。","Yes: the last queen of the Australs saved the bird that lives only here.":"对：南方群岛最后一位女王救下了这种只生活在这里的鸟。","Yes: two of them, since {#1}. One sank, one small smiling tiki stayed.":"对：两尊，自 {#1} 年起。一尊沉了，一尊微笑的小 tiki 留了下来。","You followed the Bounty mutineers to Tubuai in {#1}: Bloody Bay, the square fort with its moat at Taʻahuaia, and the end after three months, when the islanders would give neither women nor food. Nothing remains of Fort George but a field by the lagoon and the memory of the island.":"你在 {#1} 年跟随 Bounty 号的叛变者来到 Tubuai：血湾、Taʻahuaia 带壕沟的方形堡垒，以及三个月后的结局，那时岛民既不肯给女人，也不肯给食物。Fort George 什么也没剩下，只有泻湖边的一片田地和岛上的记忆。","You found the smiling tiki of Raivavae near Mahanatoa, the one that stayed when the three great tiki were taken to Tahiti in {#1}. The islanders still ask for the others to come home.":"你在 Mahanatoa 附近找到了 Raivavae 的微笑 tiki，就是 {#1} 年三尊大 tiki 被运到 Tahiti 时留下的那尊。岛民至今仍要求其余几尊回家。","You prepared the pandanus of Rimatara the island way: cut, stripped of its rib, dried for weeks, softened round the hands, rolled into pipita and scored with a blade. The rolls go to weavers of all the islands.":"你按岛上的方式加工了 Rimatara 的露兜树叶：割下、抽去叶脉、晒几个星期、在手上揉软、卷成 pipita，再用刀片划线。叶卷将送往各岛的编织者。","The other hand lets go: <b>good lift!</b>":"另一只手松开了：<b>举得漂亮！</b>"});
